 ## Operating characteristics
-The variants were evaluated on the synthetic Lego scene with 100 training views and 200 test views, with data downsampled by a factor of 4 [S1, unofficial]. Training was conducted for 1,000 iterations [S1, unofficial].
-
-*   **Variant 1 (Conv1d):** PSNR 15.831, Training Time 363.415s. This variant performed poorly in terms of accuracy compared to linear variants, despite the goal of reducing parameters [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Variant 2 (Residual from Input):** PSNR 25.873, Training Time 306.751s. This variant showed significant improvement over Variant 1 and the baseline, with faster training than Variant 1 [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Variant 3 (Residual from Alternate Layers):** PSNR 26.547, Training Time 305.208s. This variant improved accuracy over Variant 2 with similar training time, validating the benefit of alternate-layer residuals [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Variant 4 (Deeper Network):** PSNR 27.119, Training Time 319.669s. This variant achieved the highest PSNR among the variants, indicating that increased depth and parameters can improve color output, at the cost of slightly longer training time [S1, unofficial].
+The variants were evaluated on the synthetic Lego scene with 100 training views and 200 test views, with data downsampled by a factor of 4 [S1, unofficial].
+*   **Variant 1 (Conv1d):** PSNR 15.831, Training Time 363.415s [S1, unofficial]. This variant performed poorly in terms of accuracy compared to linear variants, despite the goal of reducing parameters [S1, unofficial].
+*   **Variant 2 (Residual from Input):** PSNR 25.873, Training Time 306.751s [S1, unofficial]. This variant showed significant improvement over Variant 1 and the baseline, with faster training than Variant 1 [S1, unofficial].
+*   **Variant 3 (Residual from Alternate Layers):** PSNR 26.547, Training Time 305.208s [S1, unofficial]. This variant improved accuracy over Variant 2 with similar training time [S1, unofficial].
+*   **Variant 4 (Deeper Network):** PSNR 27.119, Training Time 319.669s [S1, unofficial]. This variant achieved the highest PSNR among the variants, indicating that increased depth and parameters can improve color output, at the cost of slightly longer training time [S1, unofficial].
 
